 "synopsis": "SLMG Beverages, which is Coca Cola's largest bottler in India and holds bottling rights for high-density markets in Uttar Pradesh and Bihar, plans to launch an initial public offering in three to four years. The planned IPO is expected to provide future liquidity for its promoters. Additionally, the company is eyeing a turnover of Rs 20,000 crore in five years while looking to capitalise on India's consumption growth and explore opportunities in overseas markets.",
